{
  "requirement": "`habeas setup` MUST configure native nextest settings in\n`.config/nextest.toml` at the Cargo workspace root so the coverage workflow of\n{cite}`requirements.test-coverage.run` routes each executed test attempt through\nthe per-process collector of {cite}`requirements.test-coverage.processes`.\nThose settings MUST use nextest's own configuration format.\nRepeating setup MUST avoid duplicate configuration, preserve unrelated nextest\nsettings, and report conflicting settings for review rather than overwrite them.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "I judge the tests adequate for `requirements.test-coverage.setup.configuration`. I read the implementation in `src/execution_coverage/configuration.rs` (`configure`, `check`, `workspace_root`) only to see what the tests' assertions exercise. I took the expected behavior from the requirement text.\n\n**Obligations and the tests that cover them**\n\n1. **Configure native nextest settings in `.config/nextest.toml` at the Cargo workspace root.**\n   - `mod[tests]/fn[workspace_member_uses_the_native_config_at_the_workspace_root]` checks that `configure` run from a workspace member returns the root's `.config/nextest.toml`. It also checks that nothing is created under the member or `target`.\n   - The same test covers a member excluded from the workspace, where the member's own path is used.\n   - `tests/setup.rs#fn[coverage_setup_is_idempotent_and_hook_needs_no_coverage_chapter]` runs the real `habeas setup` and checks that the file is written and contains `coverage-process`.\n\n2. **Route each executed test attempt through the per-process collector.**\n   - `native_settings_inheritance_and_precedence` runs `check` on the generated config for profile `ci` and on inheriting profiles. The check proves an unconditional first `run-wrapper` rule with filter `all()` and no platform.\n   - The same test rejects the following:\n     - a rule with a narrower filter or a platform;\n     - an inheritance cycle;\n     - a wrong command (`wrong` in place of `coverage-process`);\n     - a wrong `target-runner`.\n   - It also checks that a child profile's own wrapper rule overrides a conflicting parent rule.\n\n3. **Use nextest's own configuration format.**\n   - The generated text is validated structurally by `check`. It requires `experimental` to contain `wrapper-scripts`, a `scripts.wrapper.habeas-coverage` table with command `[\"habeas\",\"coverage-process\"]` and `target-runner = \"within-wrapper\"`, and a `profile.default.scripts` run-wrapper rule.\n   - Tests assert that this check passes on the output of `configure`. I found no test that runs real nextest against the file.\n\n4. **Repeating setup avoids duplicate configuration.**\n   - The unit test asserts `configure` on its own output returns identical text.\n   - The CLI test runs `habeas setup` twice and asserts that `.config/nextest.toml` is byte-identical.\n\n5. **Repeating setup preserves unrelated nextest settings.**\n   - The unit test seeds `experimental = ['setup-scripts']`, `retries = 2`, and a setup-script rule. It asserts that all three survive `configure`.\n   - Other CLI tests assert that the coverage chapter and `SUMMARY.md` are left alone.\n\n6. **Report conflicting settings for review rather than overwrite them.**\n   - `setup_conflicts_name_the_setting_and_preserve_existing_native_configuration` covers six conflicts:\n     - a wrong collector command;\n     - a wrong `target-runner`;\n     - `experimental` of the wrong type;\n     - `scripts` of the wrong type;\n     - `profile.default.scripts` of the wrong type;\n     - a conflicting `run-wrapper` rule.\n   - For each, it asserts that the error names the setting and `.config/nextest.toml`, and that the file is unchanged.\n   - `tests/setup.rs#fn[setup_reports_a_conflicting_nextest_wrapper_without_writing_project_files]` does this end to end through the CLI. It asserts a failing exit status, stderr naming the file and setting, and no change to the config, `book.toml`, `SUMMARY.md` or `Cargo.toml`. It also asserts that no coverage chapter or `tests/habeas.rs` is created.\n   - `coverage_setup_is_idempotent_and_hook_needs_no_coverage_chapter` also rewrites the file with a conflicting filter and asserts it is not overwritten.\n\n**Gaps considered**\n\n- I found no unresolved gap.\n- Some branches have no direct test, such as converting an inline-table `scripts` array to an array of tables. The requirement does not single these out as separate obligations.\n- Another example is a pre-existing `experimental` array that already contains `wrapper-scripts`. The idempotency tests exercise this by re-running on generated output.\n\nEvery obligation has a test that exercises it and asserts its outcome, and the tests carry `{test}` references to the subject.",
  "references": "30d4b59c05997efd61bb4131c2b688ad67924c0439fb900eebf1ea14e56a2062",
